[7] Repo transfer
  prime values -> irreducibility is a finite witness channel (Singh/Murty).
  irreducible + fixed divisor 1 -> prime values is the Bunyakovsky direction.
  prime -> irreducible polynomial is the Cohn digit-place channel.
  reducibility over Z -> recombination of looser atoms is the RFR channel.
  Tournament analogue: vertices should be witness slots or factor atoms;
  a Hamiltonian path is a recombination order, and directed cycles mark
  incompatible side-channel commitments.
